(4) Meaning 2, a polite word for sex: the box on a form
(5) Meaning 3, social roles: behaviour expected of each sex (Oakley)
(6) Meaning 4, identity: a person's inner sense of self (Stoller)
(7) Meaning 5, performance: something we do again and again (Butler)
(8) Meaning 6, institution: gender organises all of society (Lorber)
(9) Meaning 7, power: a main way of showing who rules (Scott)
(10) Meaning 8, policy label: mainstreaming and budgeting; risk of losing its edge
